  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Easywind**: rare: 14 archived performances [7]\n- **William Tells Bridge**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2019-11-05.NewmanKMR82is** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 186 min [1]\n- **DeadCo2019-11-05.travitz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: source not stated; 20 songs; 185 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [2]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls it a good, clean audience recording and notes it is the only one on the Archive [5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taper positioned at the back of the general admission pit at NYCB Live at Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum [2]\n- Reviewer says Travis Bean attended the show that night [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2019-11-05.NewmanKMR82is**: taped by Jon Pasternak; transferred by StPatric; source: AUD OTS Front Row > DFC > Newman KMR82is > Oade M248 > SD722 24/48 [1]\n- **DeadCo2019-11-05.travitz.schoepsCMC64v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64's>Schoeps VMS5u>Sound Devices 744t [2]. Also: Recorded by Jeff Travitz; edited in Soundforge Pro 13, split in CDWAV, converted to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by charbor74.blogspot.com: [Dead & Company Nassau Coliseum 11/5/2019 Past Show Blog Entry](https://charbor74.blogspot.com/2020/02/dead-company-nassau-coliseum-1152019.html) [8]",
